Subject: [PATCH] Let a PowerDNS record whose content holds a slash be deleted and updated

An identifier is TYPE/NAME=CONTENT, and _parse_identifier split it at every
slash.  The base64 of a DKIM key holds slashes, so the content came back cut
at its first slash, delete_record matched no record, and update_record added
a second record beside the first.  It splits once at the first slash, and
once at the first equals sign after it, because a name holds neither.

---
--- a/usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/lexicon/_private/providers/powerdns.py
+++ b/usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/lexicon/_private/providers/powerdns.py
@@ -116,11 +116,10 @@
         return f"{rtype}/{name}={content}"
 
     def _parse_identifier(self, identifier):
-        parts = identifier.split("/")
-        rtype = parts[0]
-        parts = parts[1].split("=")
-        name = parts[0]
-        content = "=".join(parts[1:])
+        # Split once at each, because the content can hold either character,
+        # as the base64 of a DKIM key does.  A name holds neither.
+        rtype, rest = identifier.split("/", 1)
+        name, content = rest.split("=", 1)
         return rtype, name, content
 
     def list_records(self, rtype=None, name=None, content=None):
